iter 179 -- CH_MaxWeight (mode=1) is 3.1x AndAssoc, cracks mccune
================================================================

After exhausting low-leverage micro-opts (cp_subterm_at threading,
LPO var-set pretest, push-norm memo, UNF_MEMO size sweep) for zero or
negative gain, the structural lever was the CP-weight heuristic itself.

Engine default cp_weight_mode = ATP_CP_WEIGHT_GT (ordering-directed:
greater side's weight when CP orients, sum otherwise).  Sweeping all 14
modes at 15s on AndAssoc revealed CH_MaxWeight (mode=1, max(|lhs|,|rhs|)
symbol count) dominates on the Wolfram-axiom WL bench.

MEASUREMENTS (WALDMEISTER preset, KBO ordering, 30s wall):

  goal         mode=GT (was)      mode=MAX (new)         delta
  andassoc       421 r / 30s        1307 r / 30s         3.1x
  wolfram        352 r / 15s         997 r / 15s         2.8x
  mccune         not proved 60s     PROVED in 11.3s      cracks
  robbins       7468 r / 60s        2880 r / 60s         worse (open)
  cpl1/thm/chain3/chain4  PROVED   PROVED               clean

5-run AndAssoc reproducibility (new preset):
  1307, 1310, 1307, 1310, 1308 -- variance 3 (0.2%).

mccune is the qualitative test: GT does not prove it at 60s; MAX
cracks in 11.3s.  The ordering-directed GT heuristic over-prefers
short-but-large-side CPs that the saturator can't close; CH_MaxWeight
captures the WM-style "smaller largest side" intuition.

