iter 185 -- 9.5x gap profiling (post-perm_sub)
================================================================

Faithful WM port now proves AndAssoc.  Remaining gap to wmcli:
  thvm: ~100-130s (system load varies)
  wmcli: 10.35s
  9.5-12x slower wall

Profile of the cracking run:
  cp-gen      40.5s (41%)
  push-norm   33.7s (34%)
  interreduce 19.6s (20%)
  unorient-step 52.7s overlap (11.5M calls, 94% wasted, 58% memo-hit)
  LPO compute: 3.2B calls in 99.7s (32M/sec, ~30ns each)
  unorientable rules: 150/455 = 33% (was 64-68% pre-perm_sub)

PROBES EXHAUSTED THIS ITERATION:
  - UNF_MEMO_BITS 16->20: +9% rules at 60s on AndAssoc, but
    REGRESSES mccune (no longer proves at 30s).  Cache-locality
    workload-dependent; can't change default.
  - cp_set_ir_period: WM default = 16, thvm = 16.  At parity.

REMAINING STRUCTURAL DIFFERENCES vs WM (not yet ported):
  - K-D Heap with alternating dimension selection (WM uses 2D heap;
    thvm uses 1D + post-hoc FIFO modulo).  CP-selection trajectory
    differs.
  - AC-symbol declaration: WM's GZ_ACVerzichtbar gates on
    SO_IstACSymbol; thvm has no AC-symbol marking, so perm_sub is
    all-or-nothing per problem (mccune regression).
  - Stichpunkt (sample-point) schedule: WM has 16 pre-tuned
    strength-bit combinations for CP-set interreduce; thvm runs the
    single all-or-nothing pass.

The lpo_flat_rec_compute body is ~20-30ns per call -- 32M/sec.
Single per-call optimization (no obvious lever found here).
The CALL COUNT is the lever; reducing unorient_step (52% of wall)
would directly cut LPO compute.

NEXT REAL TASK (multi-iteration):
