  AndAssoc: PROVED 93-135s (system-load-dependent), 455 rules
  mccune:   PROVED 10.9s, 214 rules (same config, just goal=mccune)

REMAINING 9-12x WALL GAP vs wmcli (10.35s, 1673 rules):
  - LPO compute is 50% of CPU at 30ns/call -- per-call already tight
  - 11.5M unorient-step calls/wall, 52s spent
  - Reducing LPO calls = reducing unorient_step calls
  - Per-position negative memo (workflow finding #3) attempted twice;
    trajectory diverges with seemingly-sound caching.  Real bug
    unclear -- needs separate bisection arc.
  - FIFO scan (sel_ratio=51, O(n_cps) per fifo pick) is NOT a
    bottleneck in profiles -- ~200 scans per cracking run.
  - cp_set_ir_period: 16 is the cracker; 24/32 accumulate more rules
    but divert off the cracker path.

OBSERVED PATTERN: optimizations that ACCUMULATE RULES FASTER
sometimes divert from the cracker path.  The specific cracking
trajectory is sensitive to:
  - Selection ratio
  - cp_set_ir_period
  - unf_memo size (cache locality + trajectory)
  - perm_sub mask

This iteration: profile + sweep period -- no committable win.
Two structural commits this session stand.

